## Why This Is Asked
This tests how a junior engineer models read-only environments, data sourcing, and per-env state management without touching prod resources. It mirrors real-world patterns at scale at top tech companies.

## Key Concepts
- Terraform data sources for read-only references
- Per-env backends to segregate state
- Avoiding resource creation in isolated environments

## Code Example
```javascript
data "aws_vpc" "inventory" {
  filter {
    name   = "tag:Environment"
    values = ["inventory"]
  }
}
data "aws_subnet" "inventory" {
  filter {
    name   = "vpc-id"
    values = [data.aws_vpc.inventory.id]
  }
}
```

```javascript
terraform {
  backend "s3" {
    bucket = "tf-state"
    key    = "inventory/terraform.tfstate"
    region = "us-east-1"
  }
}
```

```javascript
output "inventory_vpc_id" { value = data.aws_vpc.inventory.id }
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you verify that inventory plans never propose changes to prod data? 
- How would you automate inclusion of inventory in CI without accidentally applying prod changes?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests cross-repo data sharing and multi-region provider patterns, plus a practical gating approach to prevent drift.

## Key Concepts
- Provider aliasing across regions
- data.terraform_remote_state for read-only cross-repo data
- Per-region backends and workflows
- CI policy gates to enforce drift checks and approvals
- Cross-region resource referencing of VPC/subnet IDs

## Code Example
```javascript
terraform {
  required_version = ">= 1.3"
}
provider "aws" {
  alias  = "east"
  region = "us-east-1"
}
provider "aws" {
  alias  = "west"
  region = "us-west-2"
}
data "terraform_remote_state" "net" {
  backend = "s3"
  config = {
    bucket = "infra-network-bucket"
    key    = "network/us-east-1/terraform.tfstate"
    region = "us-east-1"
  }
}
# usage
resource "aws_instance" "web" {
  provider    = aws.west
  ami         = "ami-0abcdef1234567890"
  subnet_id   = data.terraform_remote_state.net.outputs.public_subnet_id
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test drift detection across repos? 
- How would you handle regional failover and state restoration?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests practical understanding of per-env isolation using workspaces, ensuring policy via gates, not just code.

## Key Concepts
- Terraform workspaces
- GCS backend prefixing
- Wrapper modules for consistent labeling
- GitHub Actions plan gating with json + jq

## Code Example
```javascript
// wrappers/env_wrap/main.tf (skeleton)
variable 'environment' {}
variable 'cost_center' {}
```
```javascript
// backend.tf (skeleton)
terraform {
  backend 'gcs' {
    bucket = tf_state_bucket
    prefix = terraform/${terraform_workspace}
  }
}
```
```javascript
// gate.sh (skeleton)
terraform init
terraform plan -out=tfplan
PLAN_JSON=$(terraform show -json tfplan)
# simple policy: if changes exist beyond tag updates, fail
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you enforce per-environment IAM changes safely?
- How would you extend the gate to support selective resource types?

This question validates the ability to compose modules with environment-driven data while avoiding duplication and maintaining clean state separation. It covers essential skills including Terraform's external data source and locals for environment-specific configuration, for_each to create per-environment resources from a map, wrapper modules for consistent tagging (Environment, CostCenter), per-environment backend configuration for isolated state, and CI gates with fmt/validate/tflint.

## Code Example
```terraform
# ip_allocations.json
{
  "dev": "10.0.0.0/16",
  "stage": "10.1.0.0/16",
  "prod": "10.2.0.0/16"
}
```

```terraform
# main.tf (external data source + locals + subnet module usage)
data "external" "ip_allocations" {
  program = ["python3", "${path.module}/read_ip_allocations.py"]
}

locals {
  env_cidr = jsondecode(data.external.ip_allocations.result)
}

module "subnets" {
  source   = "./modules/subnets"
  for_each = toset(["dev", "stage", "prod"])

  vpc_id     = module.vpc.vpc_id
  cidr_block = local.env_cidr[each.key]
  environment = each.key
}
```

```terraform
# wrapper module (tags)
# modules/vpc-wrapper/main.tf
locals {
  default_tags = {
    Environment = var.environment
    CostCenter  = var.cost_center
  }
}

module "vpc" {
  source = "../shared-vpc"

  tags = merge(local.default_tags, var.extra_tags)
}
```

```terraform
# backend.tf (per-environment)
terraform {
  backend "s3" {
    key = "${var.environment}/terraform.tfstate"
  }
}
```
